-- Agreed tests (verification step 2, plain SQL on PostgreSQL) for WideWorldImporters Integration.GetSaleUpdates.
-- GENERATED by npm run agreed-tests -- --object Integration.GetSaleUpdates. Do not edit by hand: change the fixed cases
-- in the object's spec, recapture, and review tests/WideWorldImporters/Integration.GetSaleUpdates.expected.json.
-- Expected results were captured from the original T-SQL on SQL Server and are reviewed at step 5.
-- Rows are compared as a multiset; the PostgreSQL script also asserts the order of the order key (WWI Invoice ID), which the source guarantees.
-- Prerequisites: the spec's tables created and the final conversion deployed.
-- Each case is one transaction and always rolls back.

-- @case 1: dry and chiller lines split Quantity; Total Excluding Tax = ExtendedPrice - TaxAmount; UnitPrice and delivery time NULL kept; city from the customer, not the bill-to; a missing bill-to customer drops the invoice; window edges to the microsecond; a line newer than its invoice counts
BEGIN;
